{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00287",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.31,
      "end_seconds": 2.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "Hello. Right, let's get started."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.3,
      "end_seconds": 5.19,
      "duration_seconds": 0.89,
      "text": "Hi. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 8.99,
      "end_seconds": 13.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "Hello, doctor, I came in with them, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 14.35,
      "end_seconds": 15.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "Right, was parking alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 17.53,
      "end_seconds": 21.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Not great, I ended up a few streets away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.89,
      "end_seconds": 24.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Okay, what's been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 26.18,
      "end_seconds": 32.84,
      "duration_seconds": 6.66,
      "text": "Okay, so it's pain in my right ear, doctor. She didn't want to come, but I insisted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.32,
      "end_seconds": 35.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "How long has this been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.95,
      "end_seconds": 39.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "It's been about four days, I'm fairly sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.43,
      "end_seconds": 43.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Mm-hm. How bad is it, would you say?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.6,
      "end_seconds": 45.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "Moderate, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.13,
      "end_seconds": 49.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "What's the pattern, is it there all day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.75,
      "end_seconds": 60.11,
      "duration_seconds": 9.36,
      "text": "I'd say all the time. I've also had muffled hearing, for two weeks. There's a runny nose before it started as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.2,
      "end_seconds": 62.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "Have you had any dizziness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.73,
      "end_seconds": 65.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "No, no dizziness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 65.88,
      "end_seconds": 70.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.94,
      "text": "Uh, actually, doctor, I did notice dizziness. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.34,
      "end_seconds": 77.69,
      "duration_seconds": 5.35,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.92,
      "end_seconds": 88.25,
      "duration_seconds": 9.33,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Have you had any recent swim, swelling behind the ear or facial weakness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.71,
      "end_seconds": 92.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Uh, no, none of those."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.81,
      "end_seconds": 98.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.73,
      "end_seconds": 102.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "Nothing there, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 103.71,
      "end_seconds": 104.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.13,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.46,
      "end_seconds": 108.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Just my gallbladder removed, in 2016."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.62,
      "end_seconds": 112.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "Give me a second, I'm just scrolling back through your chart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.81,
      "end_seconds": 113.69,
      "duration_seconds": 0.88,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.97,
      "end_seconds": 132.39,
      "duration_seconds": 5.42,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. Anyone in the family with similar problems or other conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.77,
      "end_seconds": 134.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "My father had a heart attack."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.8,
      "end_seconds": 139.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 140.17,
      "end_seconds": 144.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "Asthma, for two years. I have anxiety, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.98,
      "end_seconds": 153.61,
      "duration_seconds": 7.63,
      "text": "Okay, I'm following. Okay, anxiety, that's already on your record. Good to know. What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.14,
      "end_seconds": 156.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Not that I know, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.57,
      "end_seconds": 160.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "Has anything about your daily routine changed lately?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.65,
      "end_seconds": 176.95,
      "duration_seconds": 16.3,
      "text": "Not really, the days are pretty much the same, work and home, and I've been trying to fit appointments in around my schedule, which isn't always easy, so I'm glad we could find a time today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.77,
      "end_seconds": 180.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "What medicines are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.96,
      "end_seconds": 185.55,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "I take escitalopram, 10 milligrams, once a day for the anxiety."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 190.24,
      "end_seconds": 197.55,
      "duration_seconds": 7.31,
      "text": "Doctor, I think the last prescription for the escitalopram was 5 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.81,
      "end_seconds": 202.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "Hm, that's different. Is the latest prescription anywhere near you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 203.9,
      "end_seconds": 206.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Well, no, I left it at home."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.76,
      "end_seconds": 213.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "Alright, I'd like to examine you now. Please come over here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.08,
      "end_seconds": 216.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Let me press here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.32,
      "end_seconds": 234.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "The left ear looks normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.15,
      "end_seconds": 238.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "Now bend it for me, slowly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.14,
      "end_seconds": 253.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "The right eardrum looks red and bulging."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 254.52,
      "end_seconds": 255.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "Okay, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.86,
      "end_seconds": 272.61,
      "duration_seconds": 12.75,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. Thanks for bearing with me. Now that I've had a look, I can put the whole picture together. Is there anyone at home who can help you out if you need it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 273.89,
      "end_seconds": 284.42,
      "duration_seconds": 10.53,
      "text": "Well, yes, there's family around most evenings, and they've been very good about checking in, although they do worry more than they need to."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.17,
      "end_seconds": 300.06,
      "duration_seconds": 14.89,
      "text": "Okay, so my impression is this: This looks most like a middle ear infection. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. It could also be an outer ear infection, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 301.44,
      "end_seconds": 304.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Is this going to go away?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.59,
      "end_seconds": 321.85,
      "duration_seconds": 16.26,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like a middle ear infection. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had pain in your right ear for about four days, moderate, and no swelling behind the ear or recent swim."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 322.59,
      "end_seconds": 324.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "Yes, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.95,
      "end_seconds": 348.45,
      "duration_seconds": 23.5,
      "text": "I'll start you on azithromycin, 500 milligrams, once a day, for three days. That should help with ear infection. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up. Keep the ear dry for now and don't put anything in it, including cotton buds. Cut down on salt and fried food for now, it really does make a difference."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 349.41,
      "end_seconds": 356.93,
      "duration_seconds": 7.52,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 360.26,
      "end_seconds": 361.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 362.99,
      "end_seconds": 374.01,
      "duration_seconds": 11.02,
      "text": "Keep an eye out, and if you get discharge, swelling behind the ear or the pain gets much worse, call us the same day or go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 375.27,
      "end_seconds": 375.97,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 377.36,
      "end_seconds": 385.49,
      "duration_seconds": 8.13,
      "text": "Come back in a week. Before we finish, can you repeat the plan back to me so I know I haven't been confusing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 386.48,
      "end_seconds": 394.36,
      "duration_seconds": 7.88,
      "text": "So, I take the azithromycin, 500 milligrams, once a day and come back in a week. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 395.94,
      "end_seconds": 400.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.57,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. All right, I'll let you go. Any final questions first?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 401.88,
      "end_seconds": 405.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "I mean, that's all, thank you for your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 406.42,
      "end_seconds": 408.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Bye for now, look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}